Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Covariant Derivatives and Connections in the \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] Calculus", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976889187114873*^9, 3.9768892175197353`*^9}, {
  3.977098182469513*^9, 
  3.977098186708535*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e32a3f2a-fb9c-4256-a2ab-\
ff2d5896380e"],

Cell["Revised Edition", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978360547404806*^9, 3.9783605530046062`*^9}, {
  3.9783609351176577`*^9, 
  3.978360941434484*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f584eb7b-488c-415d-ab0f-\
3846a1176e57"],

Cell["Brian Beckman", "Author",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5011898003565187`*^9, 3.5011898164415183`*^9}, {
  3.970503905858189*^9, 3.970503938930399*^9}, {3.9705040303289137`*^9, 
  3.970504033015139*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8531c00f-1b9c-4144-b1cc-\
d974e69c32ba"],

Cell["Jan 2026", "Author",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.970503954212903*^9, 3.97050395891148*^9}, {
  3.972479129640115*^9, 3.9724791301125593`*^9}, {3.973546918457328*^9, 
  3.973546918968728*^9}, {3.9762809550919313`*^9, 
  3.976280957806756*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"90e60fd9-e338-4487-becf-\
9813ab59ecef"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977148675925516*^9, 
  3.977148677656872*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"578e7ca6-7fb8-431d-bd76-\
b4fe5885c110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this installment of the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] series, we \
address a central issue of differential geometry: how to take a derivative in \
(or on) a curved manifold without breaking coordinate invariance. Ordinary \
partial differentiation is not tensorial, producing garbage terms that don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t transform properly. The solution is the ",
 StyleBox["covariant derivative",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and its correction term, the ",
 StyleBox["connection coefficient",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CapitalGamma]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5da03282-23ef-43f3-8f59-e683d4197ba7"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977327877192577*^9, 3.977327934355731*^9}, {
  3.97733134555328*^9, 3.9773313602738132`*^9}, {3.977344805844727*^9, 
  3.977344822014463*^9}, {3.977648009786602*^9, 3.977648094585701*^9}, {
  3.977648773965789*^9, 
  3.977648886431883*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"099efbbb-d635-442a-91e5-\
bef6097ac8bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We begin with the non-tensorial transformation law of \[CapitalGamma]. \
Then, applying the constraints of metric compatibility ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Del]", "g"}], "=", "0"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"b0ae7300-5e50-4fc8-8077-c1186793eab2"],
 " and torsion freedom (symmetry on lower indices of \[CapitalGamma]), we \
derive the particular connection coefficients needed for general relativity, \
the ",
 StyleBox["Christoffel Symbols",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". This derivation specializes differential geometry to  Riemannian geometry \
as needed for the general relativistic theory of gravitation. Step-by-step \
derivation in \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] automates tiresome and risky \
algebraic operations for high assurance in the results."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977327877192577*^9, 3.977328021128574*^9}, 
   3.977331334704853*^9, {3.977648101984913*^9, 3.9776483582885847`*^9}, {
   3.977648451124299*^9, 3.9776485992668343`*^9}, {3.977648931876377*^9, 
   3.977649192623502*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7c4ceef5-03e0-409a-87f5-\
d568bce26d53"],

Cell["\<\
At this early stage of development, we expose \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] as a script rather than hiding details in a package. This \
glass-box approach delivers better pedagogy and  incremental validation. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977327877192577*^9, 3.977328021128574*^9}, 
   3.977331334704853*^9, {3.977648101984913*^9, 3.977648442275078*^9}, {
   3.977649216529772*^9, 
   3.977649221221011*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5d2a3e38-cf35-49d5-91d1-\
2eef83b96ca6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Preface to the Revised Edition", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9783620478113956`*^9, 3.978362048887218*^9}, {
  3.978362262266131*^9, 
  3.978362266320797*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8c5834f4-f99b-42ca-988c-\
148ab251ccf5"],

Cell["\<\
In this revised edition, I invert the relationship between comments and code. \
I break up the blocks of code-with-essential-comments from the first edition \
into alternating prose and code cells, as is usual with notebooks. The \
motivation for the original style was to promote the script versions, but I \
have since learned that the .wl script format is more flexible than I had \
originally assumed: it can host notebook-formatted \
comments\[LongDash]Section, Item, and so on\[LongDash]not just ASCII/Unicode \
comments. The result is that script versions of this notebook can follow the \
notebook format very closely. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978362055478365*^9, 3.9783621543503*^9}, {
  3.978362272738944*^9, 3.978362299865223*^9}, {3.9783623391452627`*^9, 
  3.978362739661427*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e6a1b3f9-f832-456e-acfd-\
29519cb65b96"],

Cell["\<\
I also take the opportunity to improve the presentation in some trivial, \
non-material ways. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978362055478365*^9, 3.9783621543503*^9}, {
  3.978362272738944*^9, 3.978362299865223*^9}, {3.9783623391452627`*^9, 
  3.9783627363673153`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5c4a57c3-7a93-4033-8809-\
f6e89596ac2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A .wl script version of code for this notebook, minus the prose, \
is available at ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox["https://github.com/rebcabin/RelativityToolkit/blob/main/covariant_\
derivative_revised.wl",
  FontSlant->"Italic",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 StyleBox[". ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"]
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9771500832617273`*^9, 3.9771501268724957`*^9}, {
  3.9773269695399323`*^9, 3.977326970911551*^9}, {3.978360958511702*^9, 
  3.9783609602723837`*^9}, {3.978367071238061*^9, 3.978367072670196*^9}, {
  3.978367109243945*^9, 
  3.978367112909869*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"863d214a-4d2f-4ef8-8fda-\
b92660fb4339"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Audience", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977153047020433*^9, 
  3.977153048226739*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bdec919a-8323-46cd-938b-\
759ef07283ee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This series of notebooks is targeted at readers with an undergraduate\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s STEM education\[LongDash]engineering, computer science, \
mathematics. Exposure to introductory courses in Classical Mechanics (e.g., \
",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Goldstein",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://a.co/d/aGDvq6V"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://a.co/d/aGDvq6V"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "), Electrodynamics (e.g., ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Jackson",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://a.co/d/1L0vvD3"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://a.co/d/1L0vvD3"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "), and Relativity (e.g., ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Schutz",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://a.co/d/5iVgPNn"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://a.co/d/5iVgPNn"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ") will help. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977153053944147*^9, 3.977153244196105*^9}, {
  3.977324364580159*^9, 3.977324411077203*^9}, {3.977324444683196*^9, 
  3.977324508468995*^9}, {3.977325843557014*^9, 3.977325845658771*^9}, {
  3.9773259838117332`*^9, 3.97732599552731*^9}, {3.9773260299933157`*^9, 
  3.977326044248126*^9}, {3.977649237701873*^9, 
  3.977649263969439*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0ea1c893-ac06-4633-be91-\
6ddb165c9ed5"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Except for MTW, I do not put standard textbooks in \
the References section, but offer clickable (non-affiliate!) links instead in \
the prose of this notebook.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9773258649129257`*^9, 3.977325912216382*^9}, {
  3.977326673610219*^9, 3.9773266776011953`*^9}, {3.977331695334305*^9, 
  3.9773317026496477`*^9}, {3.97734264868922*^9, 3.977342662845957*^9}, {
  3.9783607395626287`*^9, 
  3.9783607451007223`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"20adb044-20b4-426a-8192-\
436dec75131b"],

Cell["\<\
I also invite readers to \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]think like a physicist,\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that is, to demand conceptual cogency, but not \
always full mathematical rigour.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977153053944147*^9, 3.977153244196105*^9}, {
  3.977324364580159*^9, 3.977324411077203*^9}, {3.977324444683196*^9, 
  3.977324497152054*^9}, {3.977342669832375*^9, 
  3.9773426825067263`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"933e3ac1-018e-4b73-b45a-\
f9259451c097"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Transparent Implementation", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, 3.976889556697713*^9, 3.976889851295733*^9, {
   3.977097211709004*^9, 3.977097213201786*^9}, {3.977148398602599*^9, 
   3.977148408725576*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5c85bee8-6fff-4c6e-ba13-\
21ee29fd942b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In developing \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD], we made a conscious \
decision, for the time being, to expose the implementation as a glass-box ",
 StyleBox["script",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " rather than to hide it in a Package, prioritizing transparency over \
encapsulation at this stage of development. When the toolkit is finalized in \
the future, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll address encapsulating it in a Package."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 3.9768895935975227`*^9}, {
   3.9769715522630987`*^9, 3.976971581002223*^9}, 3.9770969722863827`*^9, {
   3.9770970369338617`*^9, 3.977097104142345*^9}, 3.977099003004167*^9, {
   3.9770990471939573`*^9, 3.977099055974069*^9}, {3.97714842661103*^9, 
   3.977148428181637*^9}, {3.977649286785725*^9, 
   3.9776493630066223`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3ad9d1db-a459-453c-8a0f-\
ab0ff2d3dcce"],

Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s load \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD]\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s implementation, the RelativityToolkit, directly into your \
notebook context.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 3.976889759548066*^9}, {
   3.976889789792459*^9, 3.9768898423425837`*^9}, {3.977097167947496*^9, 
